;; are recorded rather than smoothed over:
;;
;; (1) SELF-INCLUSION IS NOT A PROBLEM HERE (Joe, 2026-08-22). An earlier
;;     version of this header held these two out of the survey as layer-6
;;     self-supply. That was wrong, and Joe said why: "throwing out Juxt
;;     because we know about it & have contributed something useful to them
;;     and useful to us would be exactly the wrong move." The reasoning fails
;;     because the terminal rule is MECHANICAL -- follow the chain to an
;;     obligation or an interest -- so first-hand knowledge yields BETTER
;;     data, not biased data. Self-supply would bite only if the corpus scored
;;     FUTON leniently, and it does not: both land on :interest, as 30/30 of
;;     the desk-researched cases do, and `all-terminals-interest` still HOLDS
;;     at n=32. The survey's central finding survived first-hand data rather
;;     than being an artefact of desk research.
;;
;; (2) ADVANTAGE — :knowable-at-T is normally reconstructed from public
;;     sources with total hindsight, which is why SCHEMA.md has to impose
;;     blind encoding as a discipline. These two have a CONTEMPORANEOUS dated
;;     problem statement: the mission protocol requires the problem to be
;;     stated in HEAD or IDENTIFY before the work runs. So :knowable-at-T here
;;     is cited to a dated repo artifact rather than remembered — stronger
;;     provenance than most of batches A-F, not weaker.
;;
;; SCHEMA TEST 1 RESULT (schema adequacy): case :xtdb-text-index does NOT fit
;; rows 1-6 without residue. See :node-types/:residual below. Per SCHEMA.md,
;; "Needing a new node type is a result, not a failure."

